  "created_date": "2026-09-03",
  "claim_scope": "Candidate C9c-4, repairing both P40 reviews' P1s and the P2s that share their subject. (1) opus2 P1-1: the family said UNDETERMINED means more than one ACCEPTED certificate exists. It does not: under the current registry no accepted certificate can carry an external, reserve or terminal row at all, so every state reaching an AMBIGUOUS code today is also one no accepted certificate exists for. Six places now say 'passes every row, partition and aggregate check' instead, and a test exhibits two such certificates with different allocation roots while the full checker refuses both. (2) Both P1s on the evidence standard: _no_certificate_reconciles was defined and never called while three places claimed it was the suite's method. It is called now, for every UNRECONCILABLE row case, and it builds terminal rows and runs the terminal checks it used to omit. What it still does not do is quantify over every certificate for a state with an OPEN terminal, and its docstring says so. (3) Opus P1-2: 'the reserve, external and terminal derivation is unreachable through the public entry point' was false for two of the twelve row cases and, before this candidate's state-level gate, for any state enabling a NO_PRODUCER lane. A test now pins WHICH cases the entry point reaches rather than restating the claim. (4) Both P2s: the guard the predecessor was named for, PROJECTION_ROWS_BEYOND_PRODUCER, had no mechanical row; it has one. (5) opus2 P2-5 from P39, still open at P40: the two lane-configuration shapes are refused with their own codes rather than derived. The three refusal kinds are data now, and a test pins them as a partition of all sixteen codes.",
  "change_kind": "assurance_infrastructure",
  "risk_class": "critical",
